Z||000000||Richard Parnell||01-22-2001||01:19 PM||||I really screwed up.  I recently changed the oil in my car and for some reason used a different oil in my car.  I've used valvoline for years and for some reason used a lighter different brand.  Well once the oil warmed up the oil pressure went down and when I revved the engine a little bit too much I began to hear a horrible ticking noise that almost sounds like an exhaust leak.  My mechanic said that I collapsed a valve and needed to change back to a thicker oil.  I put in Valvoline 20-50 with an oil conditioner.  It was supposed to pump the lifter back up, well the noise is still there.  It doesn't seem to have affected the power but sounds horrible and is embarrasing sounding.  Any suggestions.  The problem with taking off the valve cover is that I have a v8 in the car and the right hood hinge makesit impossible to take the cover off without dropping the cradle. Any suggestions?||||reg||9
