Z||000002||Raydar||01-22-2001||04:26 PM||||There is an oil additive that I've used in the past. Might have been marvel mystery oil, (small yellow can) but I'm not sure. It looked and smelled more like a solvent than an oil. Kinda like diesel or naptha. Anyway, it was supposed to be good for freeing up sticking lifters, etc. <BR>I don't know the science behind this stuff, but when I dumped it in the crankcase (tired '71 Barracuda) the engine would nearly stall. My dad speculated that it might have been breaking the surface tension of the oil in the cylinders, and the engine was losing compression. I have no idea.<BR>Might be worth the trouble, but use it at your own risk. <P>Best of luck.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
