Z||000012||TheHans||01-23-2001||03:18 PM||||The same thing happened to me a while ago when I rebuilt my 2.5. I drove it about 20 miles and parked it. Then the lifters started ticking really loud. I was sooo mad, but I knew the lifters were brand new so I just drove it about another 100 miles and the oil must have pushed out the garbage or whatever. I have not heard any noise from the lifters since. Just my experience.<BR>Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Cooter||01-23-2001||05:58 PM||||When a lifter goes flat, it is usually because it is not properly filling with oil. When completly full, there is no slack between the plunger that the pushrod sits in and the pushrod and rocker arm. When the lifter does not pump up completly, the plunger is not all the way at the top of the lifter and the valvetrain has a lot of slack in it. When you tighten down on the slack lifter, it pushes the plunger down more and soon it has the slack in it again.||||reg||1
